            "notes": "# \ud83e\uddff Items\n\n [Talisman of Life](item_7ecfd3eb-d869-41fe-87eb-0bb2e82e5718) if currently very strong. Its scales with your AP. So the more AP you have, the more the shield and heal from Suzu you'll give will be strong (Same for  [Donut Delivery](item_296adb69-d517-4885-903a-ef8f3a1d6a7b) of course).\n\nIf you don't have enough money, focus on AP items you can afford. And as usual, if you feel like you're being killed too easily, focus on [Cooldown Reduction](stat_cooldown_reduction) or survivability (see optional items).\n\n---\n\n# \ud83d\udd2b Playstyle\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f Same as before. You can easily help a DPS ([Genji](hero_31fd201d-2f46-41e4-b125-9fa9e55fed46), [Soldier: 76](hero_e1ac7ef5-4648-4998-b8b0-9e3da3e60546), ...) flanking and then get back to the fight while AOE healing a lot. This build is not about WP, so use you kunai to finish kills (with headshots) or to get kill participation. You can keep healing with Ofuda, it will not be much, but it's money anyway.\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f **Keep this playstyle for the rest of the game. The more you'll play this build, the more you'll get used to your cooldowns, healings and platstyle.**",
